  "sent_to_model": "right so someone on my road is dumping there rubbish in my bin and im sick of it. dont know who it is so im going to print a letter and put it in every letterbox on the terrace. need you to write it for me, I want them to know im fuming and that im not paying for there crap anymore. not threatening like, i still have to live here, but I want it to sting a bit. heres the craic\n\n- grey bin, Greenmount Bins, charged by weight, 0.41 per kilo\n- last bill was 63.20 for 2 months, usually around 25\n- live at no 14, Aughrim Terrace, rented, bin has 14 painted on lid in white\n- bin goes out Tues night, collected Wed morning\n- got home 3am after a gig last Tues, lid wouldnt close, 3 black bags in it that arent mine, one had nappies\n- found a gas bill envelope in one bag but the name was torn off, just the terrace on it\n- fella across the road said he seen a car pull up Tues evening but didnt see who\n- its not a few bits its full bags, every week for like a month\n- if your stuck ask, ill tell you who to ring, its not hard\n- whoever it is stops, simple as\n- going to start locking it with a padlock if it keeps going\n- want it known I work nights and im not a pushover\n\n(About me: bartender at a music venue, 31, Dublin, Ireland. Length: it should come to roughly 250-400 words.)",
